>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"SATCON2","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Permission":{"value":"CC-BY 4.0","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY 4.0","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"UsageTerms":{"value":"Creative Commons Attribution 4.0","source":"commons-desc-page"},"AttributionRequired":{"value":"true","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"LicenseUrl":{"value":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Copyrighted":{"value":"True","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Restrictions":{"value":"","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"License":{"value":"cc-by-4.0","source":"commons-templates","hidden":""}}}]},"180198364":{"pageid":180198364,"ns":6,"title":"File:Star Trails and Rockets Above Hawai\u2018i (iotw2551a).jpg","index":5,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":1212564,"width":3124,"height":1911,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Star_Trails_and_Rockets_Above_Hawai%E2%80%98i_%28iotw2551a%29.jpg/1920px-Star_Trails_and_Rockets_Above_Hawai%E2%80%98i_%28iotw2551a%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":1920,"thumbheight":1174,"responsiveUrls":{"2":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f7/Star_Trails_and_Rockets_Above_Hawai%E2%80%98i_%28iotw2551a%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Star_Trails_and_Rockets_Above_Hawai%E2%80%98i_%28iotw2551a%29.jpg/1920px-Star_Trails_and_Rockets_Above_Hawai%E2%80%98i_%28iotw2551a%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":1920,"height":1174,"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f7/Star_Trails_and_Rockets_Above_Hawai%E2%80%98i_%28iotw2551a%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x"},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f7/Star_Trails_and_Rockets_Above_Hawai%E2%80%98i_%28iotw2551a%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Star_Trails_and_Rockets_Above_Hawai%E2%80%98i_(iotw2551a).jpg","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:Redirect/page/180198364","extmetadata":{"DateTime":{"value":"2025-12-18 08:02:35","source":"mediawiki-metadata","hidden":""},"ObjectName":{"value":"Star Trails and Rockets Above Hawai\u2018i (iotw2551a)","source":"mediawiki-metadata"},"CommonsMetadataExtension":{"value":1.2,"source":"extension","hidden":""},"Categories":{"value":"Gemini North Observatory|NOIRLab Images|Star trails in the United States|NOIRLab files uploaded by OptimusPrimeBot","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Assessments":{"value":"","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"ImageDescription":{"value":"From the summit of Maunakea in Hawai\u2018i, where the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://noirlab.edu/public/programs/gemini-observatory/gemini-north/\">Gemini North</a> telescope sits, the night sky is dark and pristine. Gemini North is one half of the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://noirlab.edu/public/programs/gemini-observatory/\">International Gemini Observatory</a>, funded in part by the U.S. National Science Foundation (<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.nsf.gov/\">NSF</a>) and operated by NSF NOIRLab. <a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Long-exposure_photography\">Long-exposure photography</a>, where a camera continuously lets in light over a long period, offers a unique opportunity to see faint light sources more clearly and \u2018in motion\u2019. In this image, changes near and far are captured: a medley of star trails in the sky, the hazy glow of lights from the town of Waimea, and the <a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bokeh\">bokeh</a>-like effect from a <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.spaceforce.mil/News/Article-Display/Article/4283172/us-space-force-launches-eighth-x-37b-mission/\">U.S. Space Force vehicle launch</a>. Composed of 18 photos, this image depicts 17 minutes in time. However, this image was not captured by a typical photographer. Instead, it was captured by the north-facing camera of <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://gemini.edu/observing/telescopes-and-sites/sites/cloud-cameras\">Gemini North\u2019s Cloud Cameras</a>. These cameras are typically used to monitor sky conditions and determine whether the atmosphere has good <a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Astronomical_seeing\">seeing</a>. But, just sometimes, they also capture something out of the ordinary. For example, in 2019, a cloud camera <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://noirlab.edu/public/videos/iotw1946b/\">captured the passage of the Starlink satellite cluster</a> over Maunakea, and, in 2022, the cloud cameras <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://noirlab.edu/public/announcements/ann22003/\">captured the eruption</a> from the underwater <a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hunga_Tonga\">Hunga Tonga-Hunga Ha'apai</a> volcano.The International Gemini Observatory is part of the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maunakeaobservatories.org/\">Maunakea Observatories</a>. In this photo are two other Maunakea Observatories, the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://keckobservatory.org/\">W. M. Keck Observatory</a> (left) and the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://irtfweb.ifa.hawaii.edu/\">NASA Infrared Telescope Facility</a> (right).","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"17 December 2025 (upload date)","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://noirlab.edu/public/images/iotw2551a\">Star Trails and Rockets Above Hawai\u2018i</a>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"International Gemini Observatory/NOIRLab/NSF/AURA","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY 4.0","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"UsageTerms":{"value":"Creative Commons Attribution 4.0","source":"commons-desc-page"},"AttributionRequired":{"value":"true","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Attribution":{"value":"NOIRLab","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"LicenseUrl":{"value":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Copyrighted":{"value":"True","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Restrictions":{"value":"","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"License":{"value":"cc-by-4.0","source":"commons-templates","hidden":""}}}]},"180198360":{"pageid":180198360,"ns":6,"title":"File:Star Trails and Rockets Above Hawai\u2018i (iotw2551a).tiff","index":4,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":35856970,"width":3124,"height":1911,"pagecount":1,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Star_Trails_and_Rockets_Above_Hawai%E2%80%98i_%28iotw2551a%29.tiff/lossy-page1-1920px-Star_Trails_and_Rockets_Above_Hawai%E2%80%98i_%28iotw2551a%29.tiff.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":1920,"thumbheight":1174,"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Star_Trails_and_Rockets_Above_Hawai%E2%80%98i_%28iotw2551a%29.tiff/lossy-page1-1920px-Star_Trails_and_Rockets_Above_Hawai%E2%80%98i_%28iotw2551a%29.tiff.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":1920,"height":1174},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/ac/Star_Trails_and_Rockets_Above_Hawai%E2%80%98i_%28iotw2551a%29.tiff?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Star_Trails_and_Rockets_Above_Hawai%E2%80%98i_(iotw2551a).tiff","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:Redirect/page/180198360","extmetadata":{"DateTime":{"value":"2025-12-18 08:02:31","source":"mediawiki-metadata","hidden":""},"ObjectName":{"value":"Star Trails and Rockets Above Hawai\u2018i (iotw2551a)","source":"mediawiki-metadata"},"CommonsMetadataExtension":{"value":1.2,"source":"extension","hidden":""},"Categories":{"value":"Gemini North Observatory|NOIRLab Images|Star trails in the United States|NOIRLab files uploaded by OptimusPrimeBot","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Assessments":{"value":"","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"ImageDescription":{"value":"From the summit of Maunakea in Hawai\u2018i, where the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://noirlab.edu/public/programs/gemini-observatory/gemini-north/\">Gemini North</a> telescope sits, the night sky is dark and pristine. Gemini North is one half of the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://noirlab.edu/public/programs/gemini-observatory/\">International Gemini Observatory</a>, funded in part by the U.S. National Science Foundation (<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.nsf.gov/\">NSF</a>) and operated by NSF NOIRLab. \n<p><a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Long-exposure_photography\">Long-exposure photography</a>, where a camera continuously lets in light over a long period, offers a unique opportunity to see faint light sources more clearly and \u2018in motion\u2019. In this image, changes near and far are captured: a medley of star trails in the sky, the hazy glow of lights from the town of Waimea, and the <a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bokeh\">bokeh</a>-like effect from a <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.spaceforce.mil/News/Article-Display/Article/4283172/us-space-force-launches-eighth-x-37b-mission/\">U.S. Space Force vehicle launch</a>. \n</p><p>Composed of 18 photos, this image depicts 17 minutes in time. However, this image was not captured by a typical photographer. Instead, it was captured by the north-facing camera of <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://gemini.edu/observing/telescopes-and-sites/sites/cloud-cameras\">Gemini North\u2019s Cloud Cameras</a>. These cameras are typically used to monitor sky conditions and determine whether the atmosphere has good <a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Astronomical_seeing\">seeing</a>. But, just sometimes, they also capture something out of the ordinary. For example, in 2019, a cloud camera <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://noirlab.edu/public/videos/iotw1946b/\">captured the passage of the Starlink satellite cluster</a> over Maunakea, and, in 2022, the cloud cameras <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://noirlab.edu/public/announcements/ann22003/\">captured the eruption</a> from the underwater <a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hunga_Tonga\">Hunga Tonga-Hunga Ha'apai</a> volcano.\n</p>\nThe International Gemini Observatory is part of the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maunakeaobservatories.org/\">Maunakea Observatories</a>. In this photo are two other Maunakea Observatories, the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://keckobservatory.org/\">W. M. Keck Observatory</a> (left) and the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://irtfweb.ifa.hawaii.edu/\">NASA Infrared Telescope Facility</a> (right).","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"17 December 2025 (upload date)","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://noirlab.edu/public/images/iotw2551a\">Star Trails and Rockets Above Hawai\u2018i</a>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"International Gemini Observatory/NOIRLab/NSF/AURA","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY 4.0","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"UsageTerms":{"value":"Creative Commons Attribution 4.0","source":"commons-desc-page"},"AttributionRequired":{"value":"true","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Attribution":{"value":"NOIRLab","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"LicenseUrl":{"value":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Copyrighted":{"value":"True","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Restrictions":{"value":"","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"License":{"value":"cc-by-4.0","source":"commons-templates","hidden":""}}}]},"117174270":{"pageid":117174270,"ns":6,"title":"File:The Case for Space Environmentalism.pdf","index":7,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":4229334,"width":1239,"height":1754,"pagecount":19,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/The_Case_for_Space_Environmentalism.pdf/page1-960px-The_Case_for_Space_Environmentalism.pdf.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":1920,"thumbheight":2718,"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/The_Case_for_Space_Environmentalism.pdf/page1-960px-The_Case_for_Space_Environmentalism.pdf.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":1920,"height":2718},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/01/The_Case_for_Space_Environmentalism.pdf?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Case_for_Space_Environmentalism.pdf","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:Redirect/page/117174270","extmetadata":{"DateTime":{"value":"2022-04-22 17:46:56","source":"mediawiki-metadata","hidden":""},"ObjectName":{"value":"The Case for Space Environmentalism","source":"mediawiki-metadata"},"CommonsMetadataExtension":{"value":1.2,"source":"extension","hidden":""},"Categories":{"value":"The Case for Space Environmentalism","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Assessments":{"value":"","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"ImageDescription":{"value":"PDF of \"The Case for Space Environmentalism\"","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2022-04-21","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2204.10025\">[1]</a>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"A. Lawrence, M. L. Rawls, M. Jah, A. Boley, F. Di Vruno, S. Garrington, M. Kramer, S. Lawler, J. Lowenthal, J. McDowell, M. McCaughrean","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Permission":{"value":"CC-BY 4.0","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY 4.0","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"UsageTerms":{"value":"Creative Commons Attribution 4.0","source":"commons-desc-page"},"AttributionRequired":{"value":"true","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"LicenseUrl":{"value":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Copyrighted":{"value":"True","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Restrictions":{"value":"","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"License":{"value":"cc-by-4.0","source":"commons-templates","hidden":""}}}]},"129803410":{"pageid":129803410,"ns":6,"title":"File:The impact of satellite trails on Hubble Space Telescope observations.pdf","index":1,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":1975932,"width":1239,"height":1645,"pagecount":7,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/The_impact_of_satellite_trails_on_Hubble_Space_Telescope_observations.pdf/page1-960px-The_impact_of_satellite_trails_on_Hubble_Space_Telescope_observations.pdf.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":1920,"thumbheight":2549,"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/The_impact_of_satellite_trails_on_Hubble_Space_Telescope_observations.pdf/page1-960px-The_impact_of_satellite_trails_on_Hubble_Space_Telescope_observations.pdf.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":1920,"height":2549},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/94/The_impact_of_satellite_trails_on_Hubble_Space_Telescope_observations.pdf?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_impact_of_satellite_trails_on_Hubble_Space_Telescope_observations.pdf","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:Redirect/page/129803410","extmetadata":{"DateTime":{"value":"2023-03-21 03:00:52","source":"mediawiki-metadata","hidden":""},"ObjectName":{"value":"The impact of satellite trails on Hubble Space Telescope observations","source":"mediawiki-metadata"},"CommonsMetadataExtension":{"value":1.2,"source":"extension","hidden":""},"Categories":{"value":"Hubble Space Telescope|Light pollution|Images with extracted images|Satellite trails","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Assessments":{"value":"","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"ImageDescription":{"value":"<b>Abstract:</b> The recent launch of low Earth orbit satellite constellations is creating a growing threat for astronomical observations with ground-based telescopes1\u201310 that has alarmed the astronomical community11\u201316. Observations affected by artificial satellites can become unusable for scientific research, wasting a growing fraction of the research budget on costly infrastructures and mitigation efforts. Here we report the first measurements, to our knowledge, of artificial satellite contamination on observations from a low Earth orbit made with the Hubble Space Telescope. With the help of volunteers on a citizen science project (www.asteroidhunter.org) and a deep learning algorithm, we scanned the archive of Hubble Space Telescope images taken between 2002 and 2021. We find that a fraction of 2.7% of the individual exposures with a typical exposure time of 11 minutes are crossed by satellites and that the fraction of satellite trails in the images increases with time. This fraction depends on the size of the field of view, exposure time, filter used and pointing. With the growing number of artificial satellites currently planned, the fraction of Hubble Space Telescope images crossed by satellites will increase in the next decade and will need further close study and monitoring.","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2023-03-02","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"Kruk, S., Garc\u00eda-Mart\u00edn, P., Popescu, M. et al. The impact of satellite trails on Hubble Space Telescope observations. Nat Astron 7, 262\u2013268 (2023). <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41550-023-01903-3\">https://doi.org/10.1038/s41550-023-01903-3</a>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"Kruk, S., Garc\u00eda-Mart\u00edn, P., Popescu, M. et al.","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY 4.0","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"UsageTerms":{"value":"Creative Commons Attribution 4.0","source":"commons-desc-page"},"AttributionRequired":{"value":"true","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Attribution":{"value":"Kruk, S., Garc\u00eda-Mart\u00edn, P., Popescu, M. et al.","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"LicenseUrl":{"value":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Copyrighted":{"value":"True","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Restrictions":{"value":"","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"License":{"value":"cc-by-4.0","source":"commons-templates","hidden":""}}}]}}}}